<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Strathcarron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">642</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Strathcarron was fought in 642 in the valley of the River Carron near Falkirk, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. The Britons of Strathclyde under Owain son of Beli defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domnall-brecc">Domnall Brecc</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>. The battle is recorded in the Irish annals and remembered in verses added to the Welsh poem Y Gododdin.</p></div>
